WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.455
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:09.280
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:15.344
Unit ten: Passive Voice. Today you will describe actions when the doer is not important.

4
00:00:15.644 --> 00:00:18.297
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.233 --> 00:00:22.780
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:24.432
Passive.

7
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:28.496
Passive means a form where the subject receives the action.

8
00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:30.328
The report is written.

9
00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:33.581
Your turn. Say: Passive.

10
00:00:36.433 --> 00:00:37.330
Passive.

11
00:00:38.083 --> 00:00:39.003
Active.

12
00:00:40.017 --> 00:00:42.875
Active means a form where the subject does the action.

13
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:44.995
Dara writes the report.

14
00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:47.980
Your turn. Say: Active.

15
00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:51.567
Active.

16
00:00:52.317 --> 00:00:53.654
Past participle.

17
00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:57.485
Past participle means the third form of a verb.

18
00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:00.501
Built is the past participle of build.

19
00:01:01.117 --> 00:01:04.547
Your turn. Say: Past participle.

20
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.807
Past participle.

21
00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:10.342
Agent.

22
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.244
Agent means the person or thing that does the action.

23
00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.466
Use by to show the agent.

24
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.969
Your turn. Say: Agent.

25
00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:23.567
Agent.

26
00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.016
Make.

27
00:01:26.017 --> 00:01:27.633
Make means to produce.

28
00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:30.019
Cars are made in factories.

29
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:32.816
Your turn. Say: Make.

30
00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:36.436
Make.

31
00:01:37.183 --> 00:01:37.941
Build.

32
00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.543
Build means to construct.

33
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.591
The bridge was built in 2010.

34
00:01:44.183 --> 00:01:46.441
Your turn. Say: Build.

35
00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.417
Build.

36
00:01:51.183 --> 00:01:52.150
Invent.

37
00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.161
Invent means to create something new.

38
00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.912
The telephone was invented by Bell.

39
00:01:58.517 --> 00:02:01.239
Your turn. Say: Invent.

40
00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.055
Invent.

41
00:02:05.817 --> 00:02:06.841
Discover.

42
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.291
Discover means to find for the first time.

43
00:02:10.883 --> 00:02:13.127
America was discovered long ago.

44
00:02:13.717 --> 00:02:16.148
Your turn. Say: Discover.

45
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.094
Discover.

46
00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:24.713
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.991
Visal, how do we form the passive voice?

48
00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:45.217
We use be plus the past participle. The present simple passive is is or are plus the past participle, such as Rice is grown in Cambodia. The past simple passive is was or were plus the past participle.

49
00:02:46.317 --> 00:02:48.003
Why do we use the passive?

50
00:02:49.117 --> 00:02:58.213
We use it when the action is more important than the person, or when we do not know who did it. For example, The window was broken last night.

51
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:01.583
How do we change an active sentence?

52
00:03:02.683 --> 00:03:10.665
The object of the active sentence becomes the subject of the passive. Dara wrote the report becomes The report was written by Dara.

53
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.324
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.183 --> 00:03:17.472
Grammar focus: Passive: be plus past participle.

55
00:03:17.772 --> 00:03:18.900
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.617 --> 00:03:21.558
Rice is grown in Cambodia.

57
00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.926
The bridge was built in 2010.

58
00:03:25.867 --> 00:03:32.223
Use be plus the past participle when the action is more important than the doer. Add by only when the doer is important.

59
00:03:32.983 --> 00:03:37.040
Be careful! Don't say: The bridge built in 2010.

60
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.091
Say: The bridge was built in 2010.

61
00:03:42.391 --> 00:03:44.181
Use be + participle.

62
00:03:44.967 --> 00:03:47.596
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.598
A New Bridge.

64
00:03:49.898 --> 00:03:52.455
The new bridge was built in 2010.

65
00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.838
It was designed by a team of engineers.

66
00:03:56.833 --> 00:03:59.367
Hundreds of workers were employed during the project.

67
00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:03.527
Today the bridge is used by thousands of people every day.

68
00:04:04.533 --> 00:04:07.195
It is repaired every year to keep it safe.

69
00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:12.662
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:13.517 --> 00:04:15.470
Rice blank in Cambodia.

71
00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:19.121
A, are grown. B, is grown. C, grows.

72
00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:24.585
The answer is B: is grown.

73
00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:27.819
The window blank broken last night.

74
00:04:28.119 --> 00:04:30.821
A, were. B, is. C, was.

75
00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:36.285
The answer is C: was.

76
00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:42.540
Active: Dara wrote the report. Passive: The report blank by Dara.

77
00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:46.285
A, was written. B, wrote. C, is write.

78
00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:52.042
The answer is A: was written.

79
00:04:53.183 --> 00:04:54.777
When was the bridge built?

80
00:04:55.077 --> 00:04:59.914
A, last week. B, in 2010. C, in 1990.

81
00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:06.105
The answer is B: in 2010.

82
00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.959
The passive uses blank.

83
00:05:09.259 --> 00:05:14.747
A, have + -ing. B, do + base. C, be + past participle.

84
00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.623
The answer is C: be + past participle.

85
00:05:22.833 --> 00:05:26.240
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:27.083 --> 00:05:29.663
Describe something that is made in your country.

87
00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:39.950
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:54.132
Rice is grown in many parts of Cambodia. It is harvested by farmers and then it is sold in markets. In my family, it is cooked every day and it is eaten with fish and vegetables.

89
00:05:54.432 --> 00:05:56.258
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:57.150 --> 00:06:02.589
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and passive: be plus past participle.

91
00:06:02.889 --> 00:06:08.002
Today's value is appreciation of beauty. Learn to notice and value the beauty around you.

92
00:06:08.302 --> 00:06:10.862
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

93
00:06:11.162 --> 00:06:14.476
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

